<!-- ── PROBLEM ── -->
<section id="problem">
  <div style="max-width:960px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center">
    <div class="section-label reveal">the problem</div>
    <h2 class="section-title reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s">AI tools are powerful.<br><span class="hl-v">But they forget everything.</span></h2>
    <p class="reveal" style="transition-delay:.2s;font-family:'Rajdhani',sans-serif;font-size:16px;color:var(--tm);margin-top:14px;line-height:1.7;max-width:580px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">Every session, your AI agent starts from scratch. No memory of decisions. No understanding of conventions. No project context. Just you re-explaining everything. Again.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="problem-grid">
    <div class="problem-card reveal">
      <div class="problem-icon">🧠</div>
      <div class="problem-title">No Project Context</div>
      <div class="problem-desc">AI opens your project and asks "what's the architecture here?" — every single session. Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf — all of them.</div>
      <div class="problem-after">With NEXUS → Agent reads project brain at startup. Full context. Always.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="problem-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s">
      <div class="problem-icon">🔄</div>
      <div class="problem-title">Wasted Decisions</div>
      <div class="problem-desc">You decided on a pattern. You explained why. Then the session ended. Next time, the agent proposes something completely different.</div>
      <div class="problem-after">With NEXUS → knowledge.md captures every decision. Agents don't unlearn.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="problem-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.2s">
      <div class="problem-icon">⚡</div>
      <div class="problem-title">Inconsistent Code</div>
      <div class="problem-desc">No two sessions produce the same patterns. Components named differently. Imports structured differently. A codebase that drifts.</div>
      <div class="problem-after">With NEXUS Skills → agents read how-to guides before every task.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── HOW IT WORKS ── -->
<section id="how">
  <div style="max-width:940px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center">
    <div class="section-label reveal">workflow</div>
    <h2 class="section-title reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s">From scaffold to <span class="hl-c">AI-powered workspace</span><br>in 2 minutes.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="how-steps">
    <div class="how-step reveal">
      <div class="how-num">01</div>
      <div class="how-step-title">Run nexus init</div>
      <div class="how-step-desc">Answer 7 strategy-first questions. NEXUS scaffolds your project, generates 8 knowledge docs, configures every AI tool simultaneously.</div>
      <div class="how-cmd">nexus init my-app</div>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step reveal" style="transition-delay:.15s">
      <div class="how-num">02</div>
      <div class="how-step-title">Open your AI tool</div>
      <div class="how-step-desc">Open the project in Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf, Cline, or Claude Code. The agent automatically detects the NEXUS knowledge system.</div>
      <div class="how-cmd">.cursorrules · AGENTS.md</div>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step reveal" style="transition-delay:.3s">
      <div class="how-num">03</div>
      <div class="how-step-title">AI works with context</div>
      <div class="how-step-desc">Your agent reads the project brain, scans the knowledge base, loads the skill files, and starts building — with full understanding.</div>
      <div class="how-cmd">index.md · knowledge.md</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── INTELLIGENCE SYSTEM ── -->
<section id="intelligence">
  <div style="max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto">
    <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:0">
      <div class="section-label reveal">the knowledge system</div>
      <h2 class="section-title reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s">Eight living documents.<br><span class="hl-v">One project brain.</span> Infinite AI context.</h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="transition-delay:.2s;font-family:'Rajdhani',sans-serif;font-size:16px;color:var(--tm);margin-top:14px;line-height:1.7;max-width:560px;margin:14px auto 0">Every NEXUS project comes with a structured documentation system that AI agents parse automatically — covering vision through deployment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="intel-grid">
      <div class="reveal-l">
        <div class="intel-files">
          <div class="intel-file brain">
            <div class="if-name vn" style="font-size:11px;margin-bottom:6px">🧠 index.md</div>
            <div class="if-desc">Project Brain — status matrix, feature backlog, what to build next</div>
          </div>
          <div class="intel-file knowledge">
            <div class="if-name" style="color:#6ee7b7;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:6px">📚 knowledge.md</div>
            <div class="if-desc">Append-only memory — decisions, gotchas, patterns across sessions</div>
          </div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">01_vision.md</div><div class="if-desc">Product requirements, user stories, success metrics</div></div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">02_architecture.md</div><div class="if-desc">System design, tech stack, data flow</div></div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">03_data_contracts.md</div><div class="if-desc">Schemas, validation, relationships</div></div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">04_api_contracts.md</div><div class="if-desc">Endpoints, interfaces, status codes</div></div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">05_business_logic.md</div><div class="if-desc">Rules, algorithms, state machines</div></div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">06_test_strategy.md</div><div class="if-desc">Coverage targets, test types, philosophy</div></div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">07_implementation.md</div><div class="if-desc">Build order, file-by-file plan</div></div>
          <div class="intel-file"><div class="if-name">08_deployment.md</div><div class="if-desc">Infrastructure, CI/CD, environment config</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="intel-explain reveal-r" style="transition-delay:.15s">
        <div class="intel-item">
          <div class="ii-title">🧠 Project Brain</div>
          <div class="ii-desc"><code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">index.md</code> is a live status matrix. AI agents check it before every task to understand what's done, what's in progress, and what should be built next. No more "what should I work on?"</div>
        </div>
        <div class="intel-item">
          <div class="ii-title">📚 Progressive Knowledge Base</div>
          <div class="ii-desc"><code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">knowledge.md</code> is append-only memory. Every architectural decision, every gotcha, every pattern gets logged here. Agents scan it before starting and write to it after discoveries.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="intel-item">
          <div class="ii-title">🎭 Agent Persona</div>
          <div class="ii-desc">Configure your AI's tone, verbosity, and identity. When the agent reads the NEXUS instructions and calls itself "Nexus" — you know it's synced. It's your signal that context is loaded.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="intel-item">
          <div class="ii-title">🔧 Multi-Tool Distribution</div>
          <div class="ii-desc">One knowledge system. Generated into <code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">.cursorrules</code>, <code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">AGENTS.md</code>, <code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">.windsurfrules</code>, <code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">copilot-instructions.md</code>, <code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">.clinerules</code>. Every agent reads the same truth.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── SKILLS ── -->
<section id="skills">
  <div class="skills-glow"></div>
  <div class="skills-inner" style="max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:64px;align-items:center">
    <div class="reveal-l">
      <div class="skills-new-badge">✦ NEW IN v0.3.0</div>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-bottom:16px">NEXUS <span class="hl-v">Skills</span> — task-level AI knowledge.</h2>
      <p class="skills-sub">NEXUS tells agents <em>what</em> you're building. Skills tell them <em>how</em> to build it. Before writing a single line, agents read the relevant skill file and follow your exact conventions.</p>
      <div class="skills-points">
        <div class="skills-point">
          <span class="sp-icon" style="color:var(--vb)">◆</span>
          <div><div class="sp-title">Core Skills</div><div class="sp-desc">Generated at <code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">nexus init</code> — framework-specific task guides for components, routing, testing, API routes.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skills-point">
          <span class="sp-icon" style="color:var(--cb)">◆</span>
          <div><div class="sp-title">Custom Skills</div><div class="sp-desc">Create project-specific conventions. Stored in <code style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--cb)">.nexus/skills/custom/</code> — never overwritten by upgrades.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skills-point">
          <span class="sp-icon" style="color:var(--green)">◆</span>
          <div><div class="sp-title">Community Skills</div><div class="sp-desc">Install from the official registry. Supabase, Stripe, Prisma and more — pre-built task knowledge for popular integrations.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="skills-cmds">
        <div class="skills-cmd"><span>nexus</span> skill new auth-flow</div>
        <div class="skills-cmd"><span>nexus</span> skill install @nexus-framework/skills-supabase</div>
        <div class="skills-cmd"><span>nexus</span> skill list</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal-r" style="transition-delay:.2s;position:relative;height:320px">
      <div style="position:relative;width:290px;height:310px">
        <div class="sk-card" style="position:absolute;top:24px;left:-18px;width:274px;transform:rotate(-5deg);opacity:.35;animation:skillFloat 3.5s ease-in-out infinite;pointer-events:none"><div><span class="sk-k">skill:</span> <span class="sk-v">testing</span><br><span class="sk-k">status:</span> <span class="sk-g">active</span></div></div>
        <div class="sk-card" style="position:absolute;top:12px;left:12px;width:274px;transform:rotate(3.5deg);opacity:.25;animation:skillFloat2 3s ease-in-out infinite;pointer-events:none"><div><span class="sk-k">skill:</span> <span class="sk-v">routing</span><br><span class="sk-k">status:</span> <span class="sk-g">active</span></div></div>
        <div class="sk-card" style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;z-index:3;width:274px;animation:skillFloat 3s ease-in-out infinite">
          <div><div><span class="sk-k">skill:</span> <span class="sk-v">component-creation</span></div><div><span class="sk-k">version:</span> <span class="sk-v">1.0.0</span></div><div><span class="sk-k">framework:</span> <span class="sk-v">next.js</span></div><div><span class="sk-k">triggers:</span></div><div>&nbsp;&nbsp;- <span class="sk-t">"creating a new component"</span></div><div>&nbsp;&nbsp;- <span class="sk-t">"building a UI element"</span></div><div><span class="sk-k">status:</span> <span class="sk-g">active</span></div></div>
          <hr class="sk-div">
          <div><div class="sk-h"># Skill: Creating Components</div><div style="color:var(--tm);margin-top:5px">## When to Read This</div><div style="color:#94a3b8">Before creating any React component.</div><div style="color:var(--tm);margin-top:5px">## Steps</div><div style="color:#94a3b8">1. Place in src/components/</div><div style="color:#94a3b8">2. Add error boundary</div><div style="color:#94a3b8">3. Export from index.ts</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

